Aim

To implement Docker volumes and port mapping for data persistence and container networking.

Theory (Short)

Docker volumes are used to store data permanently even after container stops.
Port mapping allows accessing container applications from host system using ports.
This helps in running web applications and storing persistent data.

Steps
Step 1: Run Nginx Container with Port Mapping
docker run -d -p 8081:80 nginx

Open browser:

http://localhost:8081

Nginx welcome page appears.

Step 2: Check Running Containers
docker ps
Step 3: Create Docker Volume
docker volume create myvolume

Check volumes:

docker volume ls
Step 4: Run Container with Volume
docker run -d -p 8082:80 -v myvolume:/usr/share/nginx/html nginx

Open:

http://localhost:8082
Step 5: Inspect Volume
docker volume inspect myvolume
Step 6: Stop Container
docker stop container_id
Result

Docker volumes and port mapping were successfully implemented.

Outcome

Understanding of data persistence and port mapping in Docker was achieved.
